{
  "_comment": [
    "ADR-092 Decision 6: the approved answers. Each row is laid out in a fresh repository and read by every reader its columns name; a task asserts only the columns it makes true, by exact equality over every row with a cell in that column. No task changes an answer: a reader that disagrees stops the task and is a question for the owner.",
    "A file is {path, text} or {path, gen: {before, repeat, bytes, then}} (text = before + `repeat` repeated whole, the fewest times that make at least `bytes` bytes, + then), or {path, link} (a symbolic link whose target is `link`, relative to the link's directory; a path starting `outside/` is written beside the repository, in its parent directory; a row's `repositoryUnder` names where the repository sits below the scratch directory (default `repo`)), or {path, notRegular: true}, {path, absent: true} (tracked, then removed from disk), {path, unlisted: true} (on disk and never added to git) or {path, nul: true} (its text with a NUL byte appended).",
    "Columns: recognised, status, identity (T1: recognised_as_record, record_status, record_id with title_line); eligible (T1: corpus_eligible); adrCorpus (T3): record | undecided | notRecognised | unreadable | null (in no list); adrRetireCheck (T2): {counted: id} | unidentified | null, read with the row path's first component as root; workNext (T4): counted | undecided | notRead | partialBecause | unsupported | null.",
    "undecided is the rule row `undecided`: the owner chose it on 2026-10-07. Rows R42-R49 were added on 2026-10-07: R42-R46 from outside probe runs at 13136e6f (a corpus with dated non-records in docs/adr, a gap review inside a record's own directory, a corpus of numbered .rst records in decisions/ directories), R47 from a catalogue entry the record-own-directory rule left unkilled, R48 because that rule, as first written, dropped a record kept in its own folder (found executing T2), and R49 because no row held a record lifecycle finds only by where it is kept (a dated name, a plain Status), so discovery by place went unasserted (found executing T3)."
  ],
  "undecided": {
    "adrCorpus": "an unreadable entry with its status as read and no reason; out of adrCorpus's array",
    "adrRetireCheck": "counted with its identity, or unidentified, as the identity rule says",
    "workNext": "in undecided, not in records, not in partialBecause"
  },
